        "what": "Observed per-cohort-size metric values (10 seeds × 12 sizes) behind the fits are only plotted, not tabulated; no row records measured values.",
        "locator": "Figure 1",
        "versions": "V5"
      },
      {
        "what": "Model parameter count and training tokens/beats per cohort size are not reported, so one cannot check whether model size is a bottleneck.",
        "locator": "Methods",
        "versions": "V5"
      }
    ],
    "verdict_notes": "Data-only scaling, at a fixed and unreported model size, over cohorts of 1–183 subjects (about 2.3 orders of magnitude). The training objective NLL fits no better than the point metrics, which weakens the 'law fits all five metrics' claim. Rows r6–r25 are curve read-outs and have been relinked to none. The study cites Hoffmann et al. as motivation but tests in a different domain."
  },
